.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::Model\fP< dim >::InterpolateIntegrationPointToCellProperty (const char * cprop, const char * eprop)"

.PP
linearly interpolates the value of the integration point property to the barycentre of element; result is stored as element property This method interpolates the specified constraint point property to the target element property\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcprop\fP The name of the constraint point property which shall be interpolated to the 
.br
\fIeprop\fP element property\&.
.RE
.PP
The results are returned to the \fBModel\fP\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Currently the method averages the IntegrationPoint variable values to find the element property value\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To visualise constraint point properties as CELL_CENTERED variables in VTK they have to have a unique value in the element = CELL\&.

.PP
Alternatively, one could integrate the property over the element and divide the result value by the element area\&. However, this would work only for scalar properties\&.
.SH "Messages"
